Chapter: VecWideRefused
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 The vec- family is two lanes wide by contract and a wider vector is refused
 at compile time. `vec4-splat` and `vec4-extract` are the only wider pair and
 only for `Real approximate`, therefore a `Vector 4` reaching any other vec-
 builtin has no emitter that could serve it.

 THIS ARM IS A REGRESSION GUARD, NOT EVIDENCE FOR THE CHANGE THAT ADDED IT.
 Head refused both rows already; what the 2026-09-09 change added is the note
 on the diagnostic naming the two-lane contract, and the note is NOT graded
 here, because `.failing` and `.diag` both carry diagnostic CODES and no
 harness in the tree compares message text. A reworded or deleted note leaves
 this arm green.

 The second row also exercises the mask width: a comparison of two `Vector 4`
 values makes a `VectorMask 4`, and every mask consumer takes a `VectorMask 2`.

Section: Subjects

  wide : Integer -> Vector 4 (Real approximate)
  wide (n) = vec4-splat (to-real-approx (real-from-int n))

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (show (vec-extract (wide 7) 0))
    print-line-uni (show (mask-all (wide 7 == wide 7)))
  end
